IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1 -- piece dg11, Subchapter XVIII:
-- section 391, "Amounts payable to Secretary of State upon filing certificate or other paper".
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. It takes nobody's point of view; the seat layer dg11-seat.l4 asks these rules as questions.
--
-- The source is the plain-text rendering de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt (not the official text). `-- src:N | ...` is line N of it.
--
-- UNITS. An amount of money is a NUMBER of United States dollars ($0.01 is 0.01). A count of shares or pages is a NUMBER.
--
-- HOW THIS MODULE IS BUILT. One rule for each paragraph of subsection (a) that states an amount, named with its paragraph first.
-- The section never says that one paragraph's fee is added to another's, except where it says "plus" ((a)(13), (a)(19), (a)(26)) or
-- "in addition" ((a)(4), (a)(28), subsection (h)); this module therefore states each paragraph's amount and does not total paragraphs the
-- text does not total (Fork register F-391-3 and F-391-4).
-- A fee the text states as "up to" an amount is a ceiling; the schedule of the Secretary of State below the ceiling is not among the inputs, (Fork register F-391-11)
-- so a ceiling is answered as a ceiling and the amount actually set is a plain input where a rule needs it.
--
-- OUT OF RANGE (taken as plain inputs, never recomputed):
--   * "exempt corporation" -- § 501(b) of this title (8 Del. C. ch. 5, not among the inputs): a BOOLEAN fact (subsection (j)).
--   * § 2315 and § 2318 of Title 29 (not among the inputs): the fee of the Secretary of State for a service this section does not provide for.
--   * § 103(c)(6) and (c)(7) (piece dg1): the county assessment fee and the courthouse municipality fee; (a)(12) and (a)(23) only say that they are not charged.
--   * the franchise tax of § 503 (ch. 5): a fact in the dissolution certificate, (a)(5)b.2.

§ `Section 391(a) - who receives the fees and penalties`

-- src:2028 | The following fees and penalties shall be collected by and paid to the Secretary of State, for the use of the State:
-- Gloss: the filer owes the amounts below; the Secretary of State collects them, for the use of the State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a) (src:2028)
GIVETH A Actor
`s 391(a) the party to whom the fees and penalties are paid` MEANS `the Secretary of State`

§ `Section 391(b)(1) and (a)(1) - the fee on an original certificate of incorporation`

-- src:2065 | (1) For the purpose of computing the fee prescribed in paragraphs (a)(1), (2), (4) and (28) of this section the authorized capital stock of a corporation shall be considered to be the total number of shares which the corporation is authorized to issue, whether or not the total number of shares that may be outstanding at any 1 time be limited to a less number.
-- Gloss: the base is the number of shares the corporation is AUTHORIZED to issue; a limit on the number that may be outstanding at one time is ignored.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(b)(1) (src:2065)
GIVEN `the total number of shares the corporation is authorized to issue` IS A NUMBER
      `the greatest number of shares that may be outstanding at any one time` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(b)(1) the number of shares counted as the authorized capital stock` `the total number of shares the corporation is authorized to issue` `the greatest number of shares that may be outstanding at any one time` MEANS
    `the total number of shares the corporation is authorized to issue`

-- The authorized capital stock of a corporation, as the fee rules read it. The shares having par value are counted by the $100 unit (below),
-- so the record carries their number and the par value of each; the shares without par value are counted one by one.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(1) (src:2029)
DECLARE `s 391 Authorized capital stock` HAS
    `number of authorized shares having par value`                           IS A NUMBER
    `par value of each authorized share having par value, in dollars`        IS A NUMBER
    `number of authorized shares without par value`                          IS A NUMBER

-- src:2029 | Upon the receipt for filing of an original certificate of incorporation, the fee shall be computed on the basis of $0.02 for each share of authorized capital stock having par value up to and including 20,000 shares, $0.01 for each share in excess of 20,000 shares up to and including 200,000 shares, and 2/5 of a $0.01 for each share in excess of 200,000 shares; $0.01 for each share of authorized capital stock without par value up to and including 20,000 shares, 1/2 of $0.01 for each share in excess of 20,000 shares up to and including 2,000,000 shares, and 2/5 of $0.01 for each share in excess of 2,000,000 shares. …
-- Gloss: the rates are MARGINAL: each rate applies only to the shares inside its band ("for each share in excess of 20,000 shares up to and including 200,000"). (Fork register F-391-9)
-- "2/5 of a $0.01" is (2 DIVIDED BY 5) TIMES 0.01; "1/2 of $0.01" is (1 DIVIDED BY 2) TIMES 0.01.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(1) (src:2029)
GIVEN shares IS A NUMBER
      lower IS A NUMBER
      upper IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(1) the number of shares inside the band above lower and up to and including upper` shares lower upper MEANS
    max 0 ((min shares upper) MINUS lower)

-- Shares having par value: $0.02 up to and including 20,000; $0.01 over 20,000 up to and including 200,000; 2/5 of $0.01 over 200,000.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(1) (src:2029)
GIVEN `assessable shares` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(1) the fee on assessable shares of stock having par value` `assessable shares` MEANS
    (0.02 TIMES (`s 391(a)(1) the number of shares inside the band above lower and up to and including upper` `assessable shares` 0 20_000))
    PLUS (0.01 TIMES (`s 391(a)(1) the number of shares inside the band above lower and up to and including upper` `assessable shares` 20_000 200_000))
    PLUS (((2 DIVIDED BY 5) TIMES 0.01) TIMES (max 0 (`assessable shares` MINUS 200_000)))

-- Shares without par value: $0.01 up to and including 20,000; 1/2 of $0.01 over 20,000 up to and including 2,000,000; 2/5 of $0.01 over 2,000,000.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(1) (src:2029)
GIVEN shares IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(1) the fee on shares without par value` shares MEANS
    (0.01 TIMES (`s 391(a)(1) the number of shares inside the band above lower and up to and including upper` shares 0 20_000))
    PLUS (((1 DIVIDED BY 2) TIMES 0.01) TIMES (`s 391(a)(1) the number of shares inside the band above lower and up to and including upper` shares 20_000 2_000_000))
    PLUS (((2 DIVIDED BY 5) TIMES 0.01) TIMES (max 0 (shares MINUS 2_000_000)))

-- src:2029 | For the purpose of computing the fee on par value stock each $100 unit of the authorized capital stock shall be counted as 1 assessable share.
-- Gloss: for stock having par value, each whole $100 of authorized capital stock counts as 1 assessable share. A part of $100 is not a "$100 unit",
-- so only whole units count (Fork register F-391-1).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(1) (src:2029)
GIVEN `the total par value of the authorized shares having par value, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(1) the assessable shares counted for stock having par value` `the total par value of the authorized shares having par value, in dollars` MEANS
    FLOOR (`the total par value of the authorized shares having par value, in dollars` DIVIDED BY 100)

-- The fee "at the foregoing rates" on authorized capital stock: both schedules, on the stock having par value and on the stock without par value,
-- added (the semicolon separates the two schedules of one fee; Fork register F-391-2). Subsections (a)(2), (a)(4) and (b)(2) use this fee, without the $15 floor.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(1) (src:2029)
GIVEN `the total par value of the authorized shares having par value, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of authorized shares without par value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(1) the fee at the foregoing rates` `the total par value of the authorized shares having par value, in dollars` `the number of authorized shares without par value` MEANS
    (`s 391(a)(1) the fee on assessable shares of stock having par value` (`s 391(a)(1) the assessable shares counted for stock having par value` `the total par value of the authorized shares having par value, in dollars`))
    PLUS (`s 391(a)(1) the fee on shares without par value` `the number of authorized shares without par value`)

@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(1) (src:2029)
GIVEN capital IS A `s 391 Authorized capital stock`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(1) the total par value of the authorized shares of the capital stock` capital MEANS
    capital's `number of authorized shares having par value` TIMES capital's `par value of each authorized share having par value, in dollars`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(1) (src:2029)
GIVEN capital IS A `s 391 Authorized capital stock`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(1) the fee at the foregoing rates on the authorized capital stock` capital MEANS
    `s 391(a)(1) the fee at the foregoing rates`
        (`s 391(a)(1) the total par value of the authorized shares of the capital stock` capital)
        (capital's `number of authorized shares without par value`)

-- src:2029 | In no case shall the amount paid be less than $15. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(1) (src:2029)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(1) the least fee on an original certificate of incorporation` MEANS 15

-- The fee on an original certificate of incorporation: the fee at the foregoing rates, and never less than $15. (Fork register F-391-10: the floor is this paragraph's own.)
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(1) (src:2029)
GIVEN capital IS A `s 391 Authorized capital stock`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(1) the fee on an original certificate of incorporation` capital MEANS
    max `s 391(a)(1) the least fee on an original certificate of incorporation` (`s 391(a)(1) the fee at the foregoing rates on the authorized capital stock` capital)


§ `Section 391(b)(2) and (a)(2), (a)(3) - certificates of amendment and restated certificates`

-- src:2066 | a certificate of amendment of certificate of incorporation, or an amended certificate of incorporation before payment of capital, or a restated certificate of incorporation, or a certificate of validation, shall be considered as increasing the authorized capital stock of a corporation provided it involves an increase in the number of shares, or an increase in the par value of shares, or a change of shares with par value into shares without par value, or a change of shares without par value into shares with par value, or any combination of 2 or more of the above changes, and provided further that the fee computed at the rates set forth in paragraph (a)(1) of this section upon the total authorized capital stock of the corporation including the proposed change or changes exceeds the fee so computed upon the total authorized stock of the corporation excluding such change or changes.
-- Gloss: a certificate is CONSIDERED as increasing the authorized capital stock only if (i) it makes one of the four kinds of change AND (ii) the fee at the
-- rates of paragraph (a)(1) on the capital with the change is more than the fee on the capital without it. (ii) is the fee at the foregoing rates, so no $15 floor.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(b)(2) (src:2066)
DECLARE `s 391(b)(2) Change that a certificate makes to the authorized capital stock` HAS
    `increase in the number of shares`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `increase in the par value of shares`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `change of shares with par value into shares without par value`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `change of shares without par value into shares with par value`    IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(b)(2) (src:2066)
GIVEN change IS A `s 391(b)(2) Change that a certificate makes to the authorized capital stock`
      `the capital with the change` IS A `s 391 Authorized capital stock`
      `the capital without the change` IS A `s 391 Authorized capital stock`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 391(b)(2) the certificate is considered as increasing the authorized capital stock` change `the capital with the change` `the capital without the change` MEANS
        (    change's `increase in the number of shares`
          OR change's `increase in the par value of shares`
          OR change's `change of shares with par value into shares without par value`
          OR change's `change of shares without par value into shares with par value`)
    AND (    `s 391(a)(1) the fee at the foregoing rates on the authorized capital stock` `the capital with the change`
             GREATER THAN `s 391(a)(1) the fee at the foregoing rates on the authorized capital stock` `the capital without the change`)

-- src:2030 | Upon the receipt for filing of a certificate of amendment of certificate of incorporation, or a certificate of amendment of certificate of incorporation before payment of capital, or a restated certificate of incorporation, increasing the authorized capital stock of a corporation, the fee shall be an amount equal to the difference between the fee computed at the foregoing rates upon the total authorized capital stock of the corporation including the proposed increase, and the fee computed at the foregoing rates upon the total authorized capital stock excluding the proposed increase. In no case shall the amount paid be less than $30.
-- Gloss: the fee is the DIFFERENCE between the fee at the foregoing rates on the total authorized capital stock including the increase and the fee on the total excluding it.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(2) (src:2030)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(2) the least fee on a certificate increasing the authorized capital stock` MEANS 30

@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(2) (src:2030)
GIVEN `the capital with the increase` IS A `s 391 Authorized capital stock`
      `the capital without the increase` IS A `s 391 Authorized capital stock`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(2) the fee on a certificate increasing the authorized capital stock` `the capital with the increase` `the capital without the increase` MEANS
    max `s 391(a)(2) the least fee on a certificate increasing the authorized capital stock`
        ((`s 391(a)(1) the fee at the foregoing rates on the authorized capital stock` `the capital with the increase`)
         MINUS (`s 391(a)(1) the fee at the foregoing rates on the authorized capital stock` `the capital without the increase`))

-- src:2031 | Upon the receipt for filing of a certificate of amendment of certificate of incorporation before payment of capital and not involving an increase of authorized capital stock, or an amendment to the certificate of incorporation not involving an increase of authorized capital stock, or a restated certificate of incorporation not involving an increase of authorized capital stock, or a certificate of retirement of stock, the fee to be paid shall be $30. …
-- Gloss: the same $30 for an amendment, an amendment before payment of capital, a restated certificate (none involving an increase) and a certificate of retirement of stock.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(3) (src:2031)
GIVEN `the corporation is an exempt corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(3) the fee on a certificate of amendment or restated certificate not involving an increase, or a certificate of retirement of stock` `the corporation is an exempt corporation` MEANS
    IF   `the corporation is an exempt corporation`
    THEN 0
    ELSE 30

-- src:2031 | For all other certificates relating to corporations, not otherwise provided for, the fee to be paid shall be $5.00. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(3) (src:2031)
GIVEN `the corporation is an exempt corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(3) the fee on any other certificate relating to corporations, not otherwise provided for` `the corporation is an exempt corporation` MEANS
    IF   `the corporation is an exempt corporation`
    THEN 0
    ELSE 5

-- src:2031 | In the case of exempt corporations no fee shall be paid under this paragraph.
-- Gloss: both amounts of paragraph (a)(3) are nil for an exempt corporation; an exempt corporation filing a certificate that DOES increase the capital pays under (a)(2).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(3) (src:2031)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(3) the fee under paragraph (a)(3) in the case of an exempt corporation` MEANS 0

-- Which paragraph a certificate of amendment, a certificate of amendment before payment of capital or a restated certificate falls under: the increase test of (b)(2) decides.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(2) (src:2030); § 391(a)(3) (src:2031); § 391(b)(2) (src:2066)
GIVEN change IS A `s 391(b)(2) Change that a certificate makes to the authorized capital stock`
      `the capital with the change` IS A `s 391 Authorized capital stock`
      `the capital without the change` IS A `s 391 Authorized capital stock`
      `the corporation is an exempt corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(2) or (3) the fee on a certificate of amendment or a restated certificate` change `the capital with the change` `the capital without the change` `the corporation is an exempt corporation` MEANS
    IF   `s 391(b)(2) the certificate is considered as increasing the authorized capital stock` change `the capital with the change` `the capital without the change`
    THEN `s 391(a)(2) the fee on a certificate increasing the authorized capital stock` `the capital with the change` `the capital without the change`
    ELSE `s 391(a)(3) the fee on a certificate of amendment or restated certificate not involving an increase, or a certificate of retirement of stock` `the corporation is an exempt corporation`

§ `Section 391(a)(4) - certificate of merger or consolidation`

-- src:2032 | Upon the receipt for filing of a certificate of merger or consolidation of 2 or more corporations, the fee shall be an amount equal to the difference between the fee computed at the foregoing rates upon the total authorized capital stock of the corporation created by the merger or consolidation, and the fee so computed upon the aggregate amount of the total authorized capital stock of the constituent corporations. In no case shall the amount paid be less than $75. …
-- Gloss: the fee is the difference between the fee at the foregoing rates on the capital of the corporation created by the merger or consolidation and the fee so computed on the
-- AGGREGATE capital of the constituent corporations (one computation on the aggregate, not the sum of each constituent's own fee). Never less than $75.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(4) (src:2032)
GIVEN capital IS A `s 391 Authorized capital stock`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(4) the number of authorized shares without par value of the corporation` capital MEANS
    capital's `number of authorized shares without par value`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(4) (src:2032)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(4) the least fee on a certificate of merger or consolidation` MEANS 75

-- The fee, from the AGGREGATE figures of the constituent corporations (their shares having par value counted together by total par value, their shares without par value added up).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(4) (src:2032)
GIVEN `the corporation created by the merger or consolidation` IS A `s 391 Authorized capital stock`
      `the total par value of the shares having par value that the constituent corporations are together authorized to issue, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of shares without par value that the constituent corporations are together authorized to issue` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(4) the fee on a certificate of merger or consolidation, from the aggregate figures` `the corporation created by the merger or consolidation` `the total par value of the shares having par value that the constituent corporations are together authorized to issue, in dollars` `the number of shares without par value that the constituent corporations are together authorized to issue` MEANS
    max `s 391(a)(4) the least fee on a certificate of merger or consolidation`
        ((`s 391(a)(1) the fee at the foregoing rates on the authorized capital stock` `the corporation created by the merger or consolidation`)
         MINUS (`s 391(a)(1) the fee at the foregoing rates`
                  `the total par value of the shares having par value that the constituent corporations are together authorized to issue, in dollars`
                  `the number of shares without par value that the constituent corporations are together authorized to issue`))

-- The same fee, from the capital stock of each constituent corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(4) (src:2032)
GIVEN `the corporation created by the merger or consolidation` IS A `s 391 Authorized capital stock`
      `the constituent corporations` IS A LIST OF `s 391 Authorized capital stock`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(4) the fee on a certificate of merger or consolidation of 2 or more corporations` `the corporation created by the merger or consolidation` `the constituent corporations` MEANS
    `s 391(a)(4) the fee on a certificate of merger or consolidation, from the aggregate figures`
        `the corporation created by the merger or consolidation`
        (sum (map `s 391(a)(1) the total par value of the authorized shares of the capital stock` `the constituent corporations`))
        (sum (map `s 391(a)(4) the number of authorized shares without par value of the corporation` `the constituent corporations`))

-- src:2032 | The foregoing fee shall be in addition to any tax or fee required under any other law of this State to be paid by any constituent entity that is not a corporation in connection with the filing of the certificate of merger or consolidation.
-- out of range: any other law of this State (not among the inputs): the tax or fee it requires of a constituent entity that is not a corporation is a plain input.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(4) (src:2032)
GIVEN fee IS A NUMBER
      `the tax or fee that another law of this State requires of a constituent entity that is not a corporation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(4) the total payable on the certificate of merger or consolidation, with the tax or fee of another law` fee `the tax or fee that another law of this State requires of a constituent entity that is not a corporation` MEANS
    fee PLUS `the tax or fee that another law of this State requires of a constituent entity that is not a corporation`

§ `Section 391(a)(5) - certificate of dissolution`

-- src:2033 | (5) Upon the receipt for filing of a certificate of dissolution, there shall be paid to and collected by the Secretary of State a fee of:
-- src:2034 | a. Forty dollars; or
-- src:2035 | b. Fifty dollars in the case of a certificate of dissolution which certifies that:
-- src:2036 | 1. The corporation has no assets and has ceased transacting business; and
-- src:2037 | 2. The corporation, for each year since its incorporation in this State, has been required to pay only the minimum franchise tax then prescribed by § 503 of this title; and
-- src:2038 | 3. The corporation has paid all franchise taxes and fees due to or assessable by this State through the end of the year in which said certificate of dissolution is filed.
-- Gloss: $50 for a certificate of dissolution which certifies ALL three of: (1) no assets and the business has ceased, (2) only the minimum franchise tax of § 503 has been required for each year
-- since incorporation, (3) all franchise taxes and fees due have been paid through the end of the year of filing; otherwise $40. (Fork register F-391-5: the "or" between a. and b.)
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(5) (src:2033-2038)
DECLARE `s 391(a)(5) What a certificate of dissolution certifies` HAS
    `certifies that the corporation has no assets and has ceased transacting business`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `certifies that the corporation, for each year since its incorporation in this State, has been required to pay only the minimum franchise tax then prescribed by § 503`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `certifies that the corporation has paid all franchise taxes and fees due to or assessable by this State through the end of the year in which the certificate is filed` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(5) (src:2033-2038)
GIVEN certification IS A `s 391(a)(5) What a certificate of dissolution certifies`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 391(a)(5)b. the certificate of dissolution is one that qualifies for the fee of $50` certification MEANS
        certification's `certifies that the corporation has no assets and has ceased transacting business`
    AND certification's `certifies that the corporation, for each year since its incorporation in this State, has been required to pay only the minimum franchise tax then prescribed by § 503`
    AND certification's `certifies that the corporation has paid all franchise taxes and fees due to or assessable by this State through the end of the year in which the certificate is filed`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(5) (src:2033-2038)
GIVEN certification IS A `s 391(a)(5) What a certificate of dissolution certifies`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(5) the fee on a certificate of dissolution` certification MEANS
    IF   `s 391(a)(5)b. the certificate of dissolution is one that qualifies for the fee of $50` certification
    THEN 50
    ELSE 40

§ `Section 391(a)(6) - certificate of reinstatement or surrender and withdrawal of a foreign corporation`

-- src:2039 | (6) Upon the receipt for filing of a certificate of reinstatement of a foreign corporation or a certificate of surrender and withdrawal from the State by a foreign corporation, there shall be collected by and paid to the Secretary of State a fee of $10.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(6) (src:2039)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(6) the fee on a certificate of reinstatement of a foreign corporation or a certificate of surrender and withdrawal from the State by a foreign corporation` MEANS 10

§ `Section 391(a)(7) - the fee for receiving, filing and indexing, and for entering information into the Delaware Corporation Information System`

-- src:2040 | (7) For receiving and filing and/or indexing any certificate, affidavit, agreement or any other paper provided for by this chapter, for which no different fee is specifically prescribed, a fee of $115 in each case shall be paid to the Secretary of State. …
-- Gloss: $115 is the fee for a paper "for which no different fee is specifically prescribed". On the literal reading it does not reach a paper that another paragraph prices
-- (Fork register F-391-3 and F-391-4).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(7) (src:2040)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(7) the fee on a paper for which no different fee is specifically prescribed` MEANS 115

-- src:2040 | The fee in the case of a certificate of incorporation filed as required by § 102 of this title shall be $25. …
-- src:2042 | b. A certificate of incorporation filed in accordance with § 102 of this title shall be subject to a fee of $25.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(7) (src:2040); § 391(a)(7)b. (src:2042)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(7) the fee on a certificate of incorporation filed as required by § 102` MEANS 25

-- src:2040 | For entering information from each instrument into the Delaware Corporation Information System in accordance with § 103(c)(8) of this title, the fee shall be $5.00.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(7) (src:2040)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(7) the fee for entering information from an instrument into the Delaware Corporation Information System` MEANS 5

-- src:2041 | a. A certificate of dissolution which meets the criteria stated in paragraph (a)(5)b. of this section shall not be subject to such fee; and
-- Gloss: "such fee" is read as the $115 fee of the first sentence (Fork register F-391-4). A certificate of dissolution that meets the criteria of paragraph (a)(5)b. is not subject to it.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(7)a. (src:2041)
GIVEN certification IS A `s 391(a)(5) What a certificate of dissolution certifies`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 391(a)(7)a. the certificate of dissolution is not subject to the fee of $115` certification MEANS
    `s 391(a)(5)b. the certificate of dissolution is one that qualifies for the fee of $50` certification

-- The fees that paragraph (a)(7) lays on one instrument: $5 for entering the instrument into the system; $25 if it is a certificate of incorporation filed as required by § 102;
-- $115 if it is neither that nor an instrument for which a different fee is specifically prescribed, and is not a qualifying certificate of dissolution.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(7) (src:2040); § 391(a)(7)a. (src:2041); § 391(a)(7)b. (src:2042)
GIVEN `it is a certificate of incorporation filed as required by § 102` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a different fee is specifically prescribed for it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a certificate of dissolution that meets the criteria of paragraph (a)(5)b.` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(7) the fees that paragraph (a)(7) lays on an instrument` `it is a certificate of incorporation filed as required by § 102` `a different fee is specifically prescribed for it` `it is a certificate of dissolution that meets the criteria of paragraph (a)(5)b.` MEANS
    `s 391(a)(7) the fee for entering information from an instrument into the Delaware Corporation Information System`
    PLUS (IF `it is a certificate of incorporation filed as required by § 102`
          THEN `s 391(a)(7) the fee on a certificate of incorporation filed as required by § 102`
          ELSE 0)
    PLUS (IF (   `it is a certificate of incorporation filed as required by § 102`
              OR `a different fee is specifically prescribed for it`
              OR `it is a certificate of dissolution that meets the criteria of paragraph (a)(5)b.`)
          THEN 0
          ELSE `s 391(a)(7) the fee on a paper for which no different fee is specifically prescribed`)


§ `Section 391(a)(8) - annual report of a foreign corporation`

-- src:2043 | (8) For receiving and filing and/or indexing the annual report of a foreign corporation doing business in this State, a fee of $250 shall be paid. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(8) (src:2043)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(8) the fee on the annual report of a foreign corporation doing business in this State` MEANS 250

-- src:2043 | In the event of neglect, refusal or failure on the part of any foreign corporation to file the annual report with the Secretary of State on or before June 30 each year, the corporation shall pay a penalty of $200.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(8) (src:2043)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(8) the penalty for failing to file the annual report on or before June 30` MEANS 200

-- The last day for filing is June 30 of the year ("on or before June 30 each year"): a report filed on June 30 is in time, one filed on July 1 is not. A report not yet filed
-- is late once the date asked about is after June 30.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(8) (src:2043)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the date on which the annual report was filed, if it has been` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date for which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 391(a)(8) the foreign corporation owes the penalty for the year` year `the date on which the annual report was filed, if it has been` `the date for which the question is asked` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date on which the annual report was filed, if it has been`
    WHEN JUST filed THEN filed GREATER THAN (YMD year 6 30)
    WHEN NOTHING    THEN `the date for which the question is asked` GREATER THAN (YMD year 6 30)

§ `Section 391(a)(9) and (a)(10) - recording and indexing; certifying copies`

-- src:2044 | (9) For recording and indexing articles of association and other papers required by this chapter to be recorded by the Secretary of State, a fee computed on the basis of $0.01 a line shall be paid.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(9) (src:2044)
GIVEN lines IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(9) the fee for recording and indexing articles of association and other papers required to be recorded` lines MEANS
    0.01 TIMES lines

-- src:2045 | (10) For certifying copies of any paper on file provided by this chapter, a fee of $50 shall be paid for each copy certified. In addition, a fee of $2.00 per page shall be paid in each instance where the Secretary of State provides the copies of the document to be certified.
-- Gloss: $50 for each copy certified; and, where the Secretary of State provides the copies of the document to be certified, $2.00 for each page of each copy provided
-- (Fork register F-391-6: "in each instance" is read as each copy).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(10) (src:2045)
GIVEN copies IS A NUMBER
      pages IS A NUMBER
      `the Secretary of State provides the copies of the document to be certified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(10) the fee for certifying copies of a paper on file` copies pages `the Secretary of State provides the copies of the document to be certified` MEANS
    (50 TIMES copies)
    PLUS (IF `the Secretary of State provides the copies of the document to be certified`
          THEN 2.00 TIMES pages TIMES copies
          ELSE 0)

§ `Section 391(a)(11) - certificates of the Secretary of State`

-- src:2046 | (11) For issuing any certificate of the Secretary of State other than a certification of a copy under paragraph (a)(10) of this section, or a certificate that recites all of a corporation’s filings with the Secretary of State, a fee of $50 shall be paid for each certificate. For issuing any certificate of the Secretary of State that recites all of a corporation’s filings with the Secretary of State, a fee of $175 shall be paid for each certificate. For issuing any certificate via the Division’s online services, a fee of up to $175 shall be paid for each certificate.
-- Gloss: three kinds: any certificate other than a certification of a copy and other than one reciting all filings ($50 each); a certificate reciting all of a corporation's filings
-- ($175 each); a certificate issued via the Division's online services ("a fee of up to $175": a ceiling, the Secretary of State's schedule is not among the inputs).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(11) (src:2046)
DECLARE `s 391(a)(11) Kind of certificate of the Secretary of State` IS ONE OF
    `a certificate of the Secretary of State other than a certification of a copy and other than one reciting all of a corporation's filings`
    `a certificate of the Secretary of State that recites all of a corporation's filings with the Secretary of State`
    `a certificate of the Secretary of State issued via the Division's online services`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(11) (src:2046)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 391(a)(11) Kind of certificate of the Secretary of State`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(11) the most that may be charged for each certificate` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a certificate of the Secretary of State other than a certification of a copy and other than one reciting all of a corporation's filings` THEN 50
    WHEN `a certificate of the Secretary of State that recites all of a corporation's filings with the Secretary of State` THEN 175
    WHEN `a certificate of the Secretary of State issued via the Division's online services` THEN 175

§ `Section 391(a)(12) to (a)(15) - registered agent and registered office`

-- src:2047 | (12) For filing in the office of the Secretary of State any certificate of change of location or change of registered agent, as provided in § 133 of this title, there shall be collected by and paid to the Secretary of State a fee of $50, provided that no fee shall be charged pursuant to § 103(c)(6) and (c)(7) of this title.
-- Gloss: the certificate of change of location or of registered agent costs $50 and carries no assessment under § 103(c)(6) or (c)(7) (piece dg1).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(12) (src:2047)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(12) the fee on a certificate of change of location or change of registered agent` MEANS 50

@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(12) (src:2047)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 391(a)(12) a fee under § 103(c)(6) or (c)(7) is charged on the certificate of change of location or change of registered agent` MEANS FALSE

-- src:2048 | (13) For filing in the office of the Secretary of State any certificate of change of address or change of name of registered agent, as provided in § 134 of this title, there shall be collected by and paid to the Secretary of State a fee of $50, plus the same fees for receiving, filing, indexing, copying and certifying the same as are charged in the case of filing a certificate of incorporation.
-- Gloss: $50 PLUS the same fees for receiving, filing, indexing, copying and certifying as are charged in the case of filing a certificate of incorporation. The text does not
-- total those fees (they depend on the length of the paper and the number of copies), so their total is a plain input (Fork register F-391-7).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(13) (src:2048)
GIVEN `the fees for receiving, filing, indexing, copying and certifying that are charged in the case of filing a certificate of incorporation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(13) the fee on a certificate of change of address or change of name of registered agent` `the fees for receiving, filing, indexing, copying and certifying that are charged in the case of filing a certificate of incorporation` MEANS
    50 PLUS `the fees for receiving, filing, indexing, copying and certifying that are charged in the case of filing a certificate of incorporation`

-- src:2049 | (14) For filing in the office of the Secretary of State any certificate of resignation of a registered agent and appointment of a successor, as provided in § 135 of this title, there shall be collected by and paid to the Secretary of State a fee of $50.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(14) (src:2049)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(14) the fee on a certificate of resignation of a registered agent and appointment of a successor` MEANS 50

-- src:2050 | (15) For filing in the office of the Secretary of State, any certificate of resignation of a registered agent without appointment of a successor, as provided in §§ 136 and 377 of this title, there shall be collected by and paid to the Secretary of State a fee of $2.00 for each corporation whose registered agent has resigned by such certificate.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(15) (src:2050)
GIVEN corporations IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(15) the fee on a certificate of resignation of a registered agent without appointment of a successor` corporations MEANS
    2.00 TIMES corporations

§ `Section 391(a)(16) to (a)(18) - record searches, preclearance, franchise tax reports`

-- src:2051 | (16) For preparing and providing a written report of a record search, a fee of up to $200 shall be paid.
