`s 391(a)(23) an assessment under § 103(c)(6) or (c)(7) is charged on an exempt corporation's certificate of change of registered agent or registered office or certificate of revival` MEANS FALSE

-- src:2059 | (24) For accepting a corporate name reservation application, an application for renewal of a corporate name reservation, or a notice of transfer or cancellation of a corporate name reservation, there shall be collected by and paid to the Secretary of State a fee of up to $75.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(24) (src:2059)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(24) the most that may be charged for accepting a corporate name reservation application, a renewal application or a notice of transfer or cancellation` MEANS 75

-- src:2060 | (25) For receiving and filing and/or indexing by the Secretary of State of a certificate of transfer or a certificate of continuance prescribed in § 390 of this title, a fee of $1,000 shall be paid.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(25) (src:2060)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(25) the fee on a certificate of transfer or a certificate of continuance prescribed in § 390` MEANS 1_000

-- src:2061 | (26) For receiving and filing and/or indexing by the Secretary of State of a certificate of conversion and certificate of incorporation prescribed in § 265 of this title, a fee of $115, plus the fee payable upon the receipt for filing of an original certificate of incorporation, shall be paid.
-- Gloss: $115 PLUS the fee payable on filing an original certificate of incorporation, on the new corporation's authorized capital stock.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(26) (src:2061)
GIVEN capital IS A `s 391 Authorized capital stock`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(26) the fee on a certificate of conversion and certificate of incorporation prescribed in § 265` capital MEANS
    115 PLUS (`s 391(a)(1) the fee on an original certificate of incorporation` capital)

-- src:2062 | (27) For receiving and filing and/or indexing by the Secretary of State of a certificate of conversion prescribed in § 266 of this title, a fee of $165 shall be paid.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(27) (src:2062)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(27) the fee on a certificate of conversion prescribed in § 266` MEANS 165

-- src:2063 | (28) For receiving and filing and/or indexing by the Secretary of State of a certificate of validation prescribed in § 204 of this title, a fee of $2,500 shall be paid; provided, that if the certificate of validation has the effect of increasing the authorized capital stock of a corporation, an additional fee, calculated in accordance with paragraph (a)(2) of this section, shall also be paid.
-- Gloss: $2,500; and, if the certificate of validation has the effect of increasing the authorized capital stock, an ADDITIONAL fee calculated as in paragraph (a)(2). Whether it has that
-- effect is decided by subsection (b)(2), which names a certificate of validation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(28) (src:2063)
GIVEN change IS A `s 391(b)(2) Change that a certificate makes to the authorized capital stock`
      `the capital with the change` IS A `s 391 Authorized capital stock`
      `the capital without the change` IS A `s 391 Authorized capital stock`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(28) the fee on a certificate of validation prescribed in § 204` change `the capital with the change` `the capital without the change` MEANS
    2_500
