          ELSE 0)

-- src:2064 | (29) For accepting service of process under this title, a fee of $100 shall be paid.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(29) (src:2064)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a)(29) the fee for accepting service of process under this title` MEANS 100


§ `Section 391(c) - copies of instruments and other papers`

-- src:2067 | The Secretary of State may issue photocopies or electronic image copies of instruments on file, as well as instruments, documents and other papers not on file, and for all such photocopies or electronic image copies which are not certified by the Secretary of State, a fee of $10 shall be paid for the first page and $2.00 for each additional page. …
-- Gloss: for copies the Secretary of State does not certify, $10 for the first page and $2.00 for each additional page. A request for no pages is not a case the text describes.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(c) (src:2067)
GIVEN pages IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 391(c) the fee for photocopies or electronic image copies that the Secretary of State does not certify` pages MEANS
    IF   pages AT LEAST 1
    THEN JUST (10 PLUS (2.00 TIMES (pages MINUS 1)))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2067 | Notwithstanding Delaware’s Freedom of Information Act (Chapter 100 of Title 29) or any other provision of law granting access to public records, the Secretary of State upon request shall issue only photocopies or electronic image copies of public records in exchange for the fees described in this section, and in no case shall the Secretary of State be required to provide copies (or access to copies) of such public records (including without limitation bulk data, digital copies of instruments, documents and other papers, databases or other information) in an electronic medium or in any form other than photocopies or electronic image copies of such public records in exchange, as applicable, for the fees described in this section or § 2318 of Title 29 for each such record associated with a file number.
-- Gloss: on request the Secretary of State issues only photocopies or electronic image copies of public records, in exchange for the fees; and is in no case required to provide copies
-- (or access to copies) in an electronic medium or in any other form. The person's side: a claim to photocopies or electronic image copies against payment; no claim to bulk data or any other form.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(c) (src:2067)
DECLARE `s 391(c) Form in which copies of public records are asked for` IS ONE OF
    `photocopies of public records`
    `electronic image copies of public records`
    `copies, or access to copies, in an electronic medium or in any other form, including bulk data, databases and digital copies`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(c) (src:2067)
GIVEN form IS A `s 391(c) Form in which copies of public records are asked for`
      `the fees described in this section or § 2318 of Title 29 have been paid for each record associated with a file number` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 391(c) the Secretary of State must provide the public records in the form asked for` form `the fees described in this section or § 2318 of Title 29 have been paid for each record associated with a file number` MEANS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN `photocopies of public records` THEN `the fees described in this section or § 2318 of Title 29 have been paid for each record associated with a file number`
    WHEN `electronic image copies of public records` THEN `the fees described in this section or § 2318 of Title 29 have been paid for each record associated with a file number`
    WHEN `copies, or access to copies, in an electronic medium or in any other form, including bulk data, databases and digital copies` THEN FALSE

§ `Section 391(d), (e), (f), (g) - exemption, credit, refunds, returned checks`

-- src:2068 | (d) No fees for the use of the State shall be charged or collected from any corporation incorporated for the drainage and reclamation of lowlands or for the amendment or renewal of the charter of such corporation.
-- Gloss: the exemption covers fees for the use of the State charged on a corporation incorporated for the drainage and reclamation of lowlands, or for the amendment or renewal of its charter.
-- A corporation of another kind is not addressed by subsection (d), so NOTHING.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(d) (src:2068)
GIVEN `the corporation was incorporated for the drainage and reclamation of lowlands` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 391(d) no fee for the use of the State is charged or collected from the corporation` `the corporation was incorporated for the drainage and reclamation of lowlands` MEANS
    IF   `the corporation was incorporated for the drainage and reclamation of lowlands`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2069 | (e) The Secretary of State may in the Secretary of State’s discretion permit the extension of credit for the fees required by this section upon such terms as the Secretary of State shall deem to be appropriate.
-- Gloss: credit is in the Secretary of State's discretion; the discretion is taken as a fact (that the Secretary of State has permitted credit, on terms), never guessed.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(e) (src:2069)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has permitted the extension of credit for the fees` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 391(e) the fees may be paid on credit` `the Secretary of State has permitted the extension of credit for the fees` MEANS
    `the Secretary of State has permitted the extension of credit for the fees`

-- src:2070 | (f) The Secretary of State shall retain from the revenue collected from the fees required by this section a sum sufficient to provide at all times a fund of at least $500, but not more than $1,500, from which the Secretary of State may refund any payment made pursuant to this section to the extent that it exceeds the fees required by this section. The fund shall be deposited in the financial institution which is the legal depository of state moneys to the credit of the Secretary of State and shall be disbursable on order of the Secretary of State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(f) (src:2070)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(f) the least sum that the Secretary of State retains as a fund for refunds` MEANS 500

@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(f) (src:2070)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(f) the greatest sum that the Secretary of State retains as a fund for refunds` MEANS 1_500

@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(f) (src:2070)
GIVEN fund IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 391(f) the fund retained for refunds is within the permitted range` fund MEANS
        fund AT LEAST `s 391(f) the least sum that the Secretary of State retains as a fund for refunds`
    AND fund AT MOST `s 391(f) the greatest sum that the Secretary of State retains as a fund for refunds`

-- Gloss: the Secretary of State "may refund any payment ... to the extent that it exceeds the fees required"; the refundable part is the excess, never less than nil.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(f) (src:2070)
GIVEN `the payment made` IS A NUMBER
      `the fees required by this section` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(f) the part of a payment that exceeds the fees required, which the Secretary of State may refund` `the payment made` `the fees required by this section` MEANS
    max 0 (`the payment made` MINUS `the fees required by this section`)

-- src:2071 | (g) The Secretary of State may in the Secretary of State’s discretion charge a fee of $60 for each check received for payment of any fee or tax under Chapter 1 or Chapter 6 of this title that is returned due to insufficient funds or as the result of a stop payment order.
-- Gloss: the charge is the Secretary of State's to make "in the Secretary of State's discretion"; if it is made, it is $60 for each check received for payment of a fee or tax under Chapter 1 or
-- Chapter 6 that is returned for insufficient funds or as the result of a stop payment order. A check that is not of that kind is not addressed, so NOTHING.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(g) (src:2071)
GIVEN `the check was received for payment of a fee or tax under Chapter 1 or Chapter 6 of this title` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the check was returned due to insufficient funds or as the result of a stop payment order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State exercises the discretion to charge the fee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 391(g) the charge for a returned check` `the check was received for payment of a fee or tax under Chapter 1 or Chapter 6 of this title` `the check was returned due to insufficient funds or as the result of a stop payment order` `the Secretary of State exercises the discretion to charge the fee` MEANS
    IF   `the check was received for payment of a fee or tax under Chapter 1 or Chapter 6 of this title`
         AND `the check was returned due to insufficient funds or as the result of a stop payment order`
    THEN JUST (IF `the Secretary of State exercises the discretion to charge the fee` THEN 60 ELSE 0)
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 391(h) - additional fees for faster service`

-- src:2072 | (h) In addition to those fees charged under subsections (a) and (c) of this section, there shall be collected by and paid to the Secretary of State the following:
-- src:2073 | (1) For all services described in subsection (a) of this section that are requested to be completed within 30 minutes on the same day as the day of the request, an additional sum of up to $10,000 and for all services described in subsections (a) and (c) of this section that are requested to be completed within 1 hour on the same day as the day of the request, an additional sum of up to $2,500 and for all services described in subsections (a) and (c) of this section that are requested to be completed within 2 hours on the same day as the day of the request, an additional sum of up to $1,500; and
-- src:2074 | (2) For all services described in subsections (a) and (c) of this section that are requested to be completed within the same day as the day of the request, an additional sum of up to $500; and
-- src:2075 | (3) For all services described in subsections (a) and (c) of this section that are requested to be completed within a 24-hour period from the time of the request, an additional sum of up to $300.
-- src:2076 | The Secretary of State shall establish (and may from time to time alter or amend) a schedule of specific fees payable up to the limits under this subsection.
-- Gloss: on top of the fees under (a) and (c), up to the stated sums, for a service requested to be completed within: 30 minutes on the same day (services described in subsection (a) ONLY) $10,000;
-- 1 hour on the same day $2,500; 2 hours on the same day $1,500; the same day $500; a 24-hour period $300 (services described in (a) and (c)). The Secretary of State sets the actual sums in a schedule
-- up to those limits; the schedule is not among the inputs.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(h) (src:2072-2076)
DECLARE `s 391(h) Speed at which a service is requested` IS ONE OF
    `completed within 30 minutes on the same day as the day of the request`
    `completed within 1 hour on the same day as the day of the request`
    `completed within 2 hours on the same day as the day of the request`
    `completed within the same day as the day of the request`
    `completed within a 24-hour period from the time of the request`
    `completed at a speed that s 391(h) does not name`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(h) (src:2072-2076)
GIVEN speed IS A `s 391(h) Speed at which a service is requested`
      `the service is described in subsection (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service is described in subsection (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 391(h) the most that may be added to the fees for the service` speed `the service is described in subsection (a)` `the service is described in subsection (c)` MEANS
    CONSIDER speed
    WHEN `completed within 30 minutes on the same day as the day of the request` THEN
        IF `the service is described in subsection (a)` THEN JUST 10_000 ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `completed within 1 hour on the same day as the day of the request` THEN
        IF (`the service is described in subsection (a)` OR `the service is described in subsection (c)`) THEN JUST 2_500 ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `completed within 2 hours on the same day as the day of the request` THEN
        IF (`the service is described in subsection (a)` OR `the service is described in subsection (c)`) THEN JUST 1_500 ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `completed within the same day as the day of the request` THEN
        IF (`the service is described in subsection (a)` OR `the service is described in subsection (c)`) THEN JUST 500 ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `completed within a 24-hour period from the time of the request` THEN
        IF (`the service is described in subsection (a)` OR `the service is described in subsection (c)`) THEN JUST 300 ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `completed at a speed that s 391(h) does not name` THEN NOTHING

@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(h) (src:2072-2076)
GIVEN speed IS A `s 391(h) Speed at which a service is requested`
      `the service is described in subsection (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service is described in subsection (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the additional sum in the Secretary of State's schedule` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 391(h) the additional sum in the schedule is within the limit` speed `the service is described in subsection (a)` `the service is described in subsection (c)` `the additional sum in the Secretary of State's schedule` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 391(h) the most that may be added to the fees for the service` speed `the service is described in subsection (a)` `the service is described in subsection (c)`
    WHEN JUST limit THEN JUST ((`the additional sum in the Secretary of State's schedule` AT LEAST 0) AND (`the additional sum in the Secretary of State's schedule` AT MOST limit))
    WHEN NOTHING    THEN NOTHING

§ `Section 391(i) - failure to pay a fee or tax: loss of good standing`

-- src:2077 | A domestic corporation or a foreign corporation registered to do business in this State that files with the Secretary of State any instrument or certificate, and in connection therewith, neglects, refuses or fails to pay any fee or tax under Chapter 1 or Chapter 6 of this title shall, after written demand therefor by the Secretary of State by mail addressed to such domestic corporation or foreign corporation in care of its registered agent in this State, cease to be in good standing as a domestic corporation or registered as a foreign corporation in this State on the ninetieth day following the date of mailing of such demand, unless such fee or tax and, if applicable, the fee provided for in subsection (g) of this section are paid in full prior to the ninetieth day following the date of mailing of such demand. …
-- Gloss: the corporation ceases to be in good standing (or, if foreign, registered) ON the ninetieth day following the date of mailing of the Secretary of State's written demand (by mail,
-- addressed in care of its registered agent), unless the fee or tax, and the subsection (g) fee if applicable, are paid in full PRIOR to that ninetieth day. So payment on the 89th day saves it;
-- payment on the 90th day does not (Fork register F-391-8). The mailing date plus 90 calendar days is the ninetieth day.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(i) (src:2077)
GIVEN `the corporation filed an instrument or certificate and neglected, refused or failed to pay a fee or tax under Chapter 1 or Chapter 6 of this title` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the Secretary of State mailed the written demand to the corporation in care of its registered agent, if the Secretary of State has` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date on which the fee or tax and any subsection (g) fee were paid in full, if they have been` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date for which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 391(i) the corporation has ceased to be in good standing or registered` `the corporation filed an instrument or certificate and neglected, refused or failed to pay a fee or tax under Chapter 1 or Chapter 6 of this title` `the date on which the Secretary of State mailed the written demand to the corporation in care of its registered agent, if the Secretary of State has` `the date on which the fee or tax and any subsection (g) fee were paid in full, if they have been` `the date for which the question is asked` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date on which the Secretary of State mailed the written demand to the corporation in care of its registered agent, if the Secretary of State has`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST mailed THEN
            `the corporation filed an instrument or certificate and neglected, refused or failed to pay a fee or tax under Chapter 1 or Chapter 6 of this title`
        AND (`the date for which the question is asked` AT LEAST (mailed PLUS 90))
        AND (NOT (CONSIDER `the date on which the fee or tax and any subsection (g) fee were paid in full, if they have been`
                  WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                  WHEN JUST paid THEN paid LESS THAN (mailed PLUS 90)))

-- src:2077 | A domestic corporation that has ceased to be in good standing or a foreign corporation that has ceased to be registered by reason of the neglect, refusal or failure to pay any such fee or tax shall be restored to and have the status of a domestic corporation in good standing or a foreign corporation that is registered in this State upon the payment of the fee or tax which such domestic corporation or foreign corporation neglected, refused or failed to pay together with the fee provided for in subsection (g) of this section, if applicable. …
-- Gloss: restored, with the status of a domestic corporation in good standing (or of a registered foreign corporation), upon payment of the fee or tax it neglected together with the subsection (g) fee, if applicable.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(i) (src:2077)
GIVEN `the corporation has ceased to be in good standing or registered by reason of the neglect, refusal or failure to pay a fee or tax` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fee or tax has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subsection (g) fee is applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subsection (g) fee has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 391(i) the corporation is restored to good standing or registered status` `the corporation has ceased to be in good standing or registered by reason of the neglect, refusal or failure to pay a fee or tax` `the fee or tax has been paid` `the subsection (g) fee is applicable` `the subsection (g) fee has been paid` MEANS
        `the corporation has ceased to be in good standing or registered by reason of the neglect, refusal or failure to pay a fee or tax`
    AND `the fee or tax has been paid`
    AND ((NOT `the subsection (g) fee is applicable`) OR `the subsection (g) fee has been paid`)

-- src:2077 | The Secretary of State shall not accept for filing any instrument authorized to be filed with the Secretary of State under this title in respect of any domestic corporation that is not in good standing or any foreign corporation that has ceased to be registered by reason of the neglect, refusal or failure to pay any such fee or tax, and shall not issue any certificate of good standing with respect to such domestic corporation or foreign corporation, unless and until such domestic corporation or foreign corporation shall have been restored to and have the status of a domestic corporation in good standing or a foreign corporation duly registered in this State.
-- Gloss: until the corporation is restored, the Secretary of State is barred from accepting an instrument for filing in respect of it, and from issuing a certificate of good standing for it.
-- This says only when subsection (i) bars; it does not say that the Secretary of State must accept or issue once the bar lifts, so the rule answers whether the bar holds, not whether the filing is accepted.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(i) (src:2077)
GIVEN `the corporation has ceased to be in good standing or registered by reason of the neglect, refusal or failure to pay a fee or tax` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has been restored` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 391(i) the Secretary of State is barred from accepting an instrument for filing from the corporation or issuing a certificate of good standing for it` `the corporation has ceased to be in good standing or registered by reason of the neglect, refusal or failure to pay a fee or tax` `the corporation has been restored` MEANS
        `the corporation has ceased to be in good standing or registered by reason of the neglect, refusal or failure to pay a fee or tax`
    AND (NOT `the corporation has been restored`)

§ `Section 391(j) - exempt corporation`

-- src:2078 | (j) As used in this section, the term “exempt corporation” shall have the meaning given to it in § 501(b) of this title.
-- out of range: § 501(b) of this title (8 Del. C. ch. 5, not among the inputs): whether a corporation is an "exempt corporation" is a plain fact. The rules above take it directly.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(j) (src:2078)
GIVEN `the corporation has the meaning of exempt corporation given in § 501(b) of this title` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 391(j) the corporation is an exempt corporation` `the corporation has the meaning of exempt corporation given in § 501(b) of this title` MEANS
    `the corporation has the meaning of exempt corporation given in § 501(b) of this title`


§ `Section 391(a) - the amount of each paragraph, by the paper or service`

-- A router, not a new rule: for a paper or service whose fee subsection (a) states as one amount (or as a ceiling), it names the paragraph and gives that paragraph's amount.
-- The papers whose fee depends on the facts of the filing (the original certificate of incorporation, amendments, mergers, dissolutions, copies, per-page and per-line fees, the late-report
-- penalty) have their own rules above and are not in this list.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(6) (src:2039); § 391(a)(8) (src:2043); § 391(a)(11) (src:2046); § 391(a)(12) (src:2047); § 391(a)(14) (src:2049); § 391(a)(16) (src:2051); § 391(a)(17) (src:2052); § 391(a)(20) (src:2055); § 391(a)(21) (src:2056); § 391(a)(24) (src:2059); § 391(a)(25) (src:2060); § 391(a)(27) (src:2062); § 391(a)(29) (src:2064)
DECLARE `s 391(a) Paper or service whose fee is one stated amount or ceiling` IS ONE OF
    `a certificate of reinstatement or of surrender and withdrawal of a foreign corporation (s 391(a)(6))`
    `the annual report of a foreign corporation doing business in this State (s 391(a)(8))`
    `a certificate of the Secretary of State other than a certification of a copy and other than one reciting all filings (s 391(a)(11))`
    `a certificate of the Secretary of State reciting all of a corporation's filings (s 391(a)(11))`
    `a certificate of the Secretary of State issued via the Division's online services (s 391(a)(11))`
    `a certificate of change of location or change of registered agent (s 391(a)(12))`
    `a certificate of resignation of a registered agent and appointment of a successor (s 391(a)(14))`
    `a written report of a record search (s 391(a)(16))`
    `the preclearance of a document for filing, other than one for filing under s 204 (s 391(a)(17))`
    `the preclearance of a document for filing under s 204 (s 391(a)(17))`
    `the documents prescribed in s 389(c) (s 391(a)(20))`
    `the annual documents prescribed in s 389(d) (s 391(a)(21))`
    `a corporate name reservation application, a renewal application or a notice of transfer or cancellation (s 391(a)(24))`
    `a certificate of transfer or a certificate of continuance prescribed in s 390 (s 391(a)(25))`
    `a certificate of conversion prescribed in s 266 (s 391(a)(27))`
    `accepting service of process under this title (s 391(a)(29))`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a) (src:2028-2064)
GIVEN paper IS A `s 391(a) Paper or service whose fee is one stated amount or ceiling`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 391(a) the most that may be charged under the paragraph for the paper or service` paper MEANS
    CONSIDER paper
    WHEN `a certificate of reinstatement or of surrender and withdrawal of a foreign corporation (s 391(a)(6))` THEN
        `s 391(a)(6) the fee on a certificate of reinstatement of a foreign corporation or a certificate of surrender and withdrawal from the State by a foreign corporation`
    WHEN `the annual report of a foreign corporation doing business in this State (s 391(a)(8))` THEN
        `s 391(a)(8) the fee on the annual report of a foreign corporation doing business in this State`
    WHEN `a certificate of the Secretary of State other than a certification of a copy and other than one reciting all filings (s 391(a)(11))` THEN
        `s 391(a)(11) the most that may be charged for each certificate` `a certificate of the Secretary of State other than a certification of a copy and other than one reciting all of a corporation's filings`
    WHEN `a certificate of the Secretary of State reciting all of a corporation's filings (s 391(a)(11))` THEN
        `s 391(a)(11) the most that may be charged for each certificate` `a certificate of the Secretary of State that recites all of a corporation's filings with the Secretary of State`
    WHEN `a certificate of the Secretary of State issued via the Division's online services (s 391(a)(11))` THEN
        `s 391(a)(11) the most that may be charged for each certificate` `a certificate of the Secretary of State issued via the Division's online services`
    WHEN `a certificate of change of location or change of registered agent (s 391(a)(12))` THEN
        `s 391(a)(12) the fee on a certificate of change of location or change of registered agent`
    WHEN `a certificate of resignation of a registered agent and appointment of a successor (s 391(a)(14))` THEN
        `s 391(a)(14) the fee on a certificate of resignation of a registered agent and appointment of a successor`
    WHEN `a written report of a record search (s 391(a)(16))` THEN
        `s 391(a)(16) the most that may be charged for a written report of a record search`
    WHEN `the preclearance of a document for filing, other than one for filing under s 204 (s 391(a)(17))` THEN
        `s 391(a)(17) the fee for preclearance of a document for filing` FALSE
    WHEN `the preclearance of a document for filing under s 204 (s 391(a)(17))` THEN
        `s 391(a)(17) the fee for preclearance of a document for filing` TRUE
    WHEN `the documents prescribed in s 389(c) (s 391(a)(20))` THEN
        `s 391(a)(20) the fee on the documents prescribed in § 389(c)`
    WHEN `the annual documents prescribed in s 389(d) (s 391(a)(21))` THEN
        `s 391(a)(21) the annual fee on the documents prescribed in § 389(d)`
    WHEN `a corporate name reservation application, a renewal application or a notice of transfer or cancellation (s 391(a)(24))` THEN
        `s 391(a)(24) the most that may be charged for accepting a corporate name reservation application, a renewal application or a notice of transfer or cancellation`
    WHEN `a certificate of transfer or a certificate of continuance prescribed in s 390 (s 391(a)(25))` THEN
        `s 391(a)(25) the fee on a certificate of transfer or a certificate of continuance prescribed in § 390`
    WHEN `a certificate of conversion prescribed in s 266 (s 391(a)(27))` THEN
        `s 391(a)(27) the fee on a certificate of conversion prescribed in § 266`
    WHEN `accepting service of process under this title (s 391(a)(29))` THEN
        `s 391(a)(29) the fee for accepting service of process under this title`

-- The text says "up to" for three of these: the Division's online certificates (a)(11), a record search report (a)(16) and a name reservation (a)(24). For them the amount above is a CEILING.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 391(a)(11) (src:2046); § 391(a)(16) (src:2051); § 391(a)(24) (src:2059)
GIVEN paper IS A `s 391(a) Paper or service whose fee is one stated amount or ceiling`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 391(a) the amount stated for the paper or service is only a ceiling` paper MEANS
    CONSIDER paper
    WHEN `a certificate of the Secretary of State issued via the Division's online services (s 391(a)(11))` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a written report of a record search (s 391(a)(16))` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a corporate name reservation application, a renewal application or a notice of transfer or cancellation (s 391(a)(24))` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
